                        "entry_id": "7923dc3e-9e98-328f-9257-5b12dc6992c6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг., сниж. вмешиваться во что-либо (в чужие дела, в чей-либо разговор и т. п.)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ec980372-c68b-4326-8580-f78d833b4fd8",
                                "sense_id": "e88e2e03-2d63-3301-8ceb-cb074add0c2c",
                                "text": "— Не должен бы ты, Лаврентий, по худости, наперёд других встревать в разговор .."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "80590750-e2be-46cb-9149-59968ae70e9f",
                        "source_entry_id": "7923dc3e-9e98-328f-9257-5b12dc6992c6",
                        "source_sense_id": "e88e2e03-2d63-3301-8ceb-cb074add0c2c",
                        "target_lang_word": "butt in",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "butt in",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5d14909-5a46-3e05-8c25-2443ef56f6a4",
                                        "entry_id": "82d769cf-348d-3a2e-8c00-5509eade8eb8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To join a conversation or situation in which one is not welcome or invited; to interject (connotes a rude or discourteous interruption)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e29081a6-d217-40a6-8708-1741cb6d125f",
                                                "sense_id": "b5d14909-5a46-3e05-8c25-2443ef56f6a4",
                                                "text": "Hey, this is none of your business; don’t butt in!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d1f3367-f636-4085-8a7e-fbd56c129289",
                                                "sense_id": "b5d14909-5a46-3e05-8c25-2443ef56f6a4",
                                                "text": "Forgive me for butting in."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f68f26f6-d8a7-4b93-85ea-9836f90f1606",
                                                "sense_id": "b5d14909-5a46-3e05-8c25-2443ef56f6a4",
                                                "text": "That spurt of rage took Bradly in the midriff before he could control it. He was standing over Podson with such eminent threat in his bristling beard that Podson said sulkily, \"Oh, all right, I don't want to butt in, if you feel like that about it.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "088625bc-c81a-3cdd-8826-2b0411e8837c",
                                        "entry_id": "82d769cf-348d-3a2e-8c00-5509eade8eb8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To join a queue not at the end, but in the middle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fe3aea43-8184-4044-9c6a-b7630345fa81",
                        "source_entry_id": "7923dc3e-9e98-328f-9257-5b12dc6992c6",
                        "source_sense_id": "e88e2e03-2d63-3301-8ceb-cb074add0c2c",
                        "target_lang_word": "interfere",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "interfere",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "63f98ec5-134e-3158-9321-68ca44631a1f",
                                        "entry_id": "31633c1b-7496-3a25-a49d-7e0bccab2fe8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To get involved or involve oneself, causing disturbance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d70eeeb-7d2e-42d0-9dae-7da59200f40c",
                                                "sense_id": "63f98ec5-134e-3158-9321-68ca44631a1f",
                                                "text": "I always try not to interfere with other people’s personal affairs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4cdaac3c-7f67-476d-9e55-bfac02a8a72a",
                                                "sense_id": "63f98ec5-134e-3158-9321-68ca44631a1f",
                                                "text": "I’ve known ere now an interfering branch / Of alder catch my lifted axe behind me. / But that was in the woods, to hold my hand / From striking at another alder’s roots, / And that was, as I say, an alder branch."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c53ec887-0d67-3f31-aae9-a107b4ec946f",
                                        "entry_id": "31633c1b-7496-3a25-a49d-7e0bccab2fe8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "(of waves) To be correlated with each other when overlapped or superposed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0046a62e-8a4e-4ba8-8da8-8b8792c6c57b",
                                                "sense_id": "c53ec887-0d67-3f31-aae9-a107b4ec946f",
                                                "text": "Correlated waves interfere to produce interesting patterns, while uncorrelated waves overlap without interfering."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70a23869-aa9a-46dc-8b1b-2e13fbaf9f7d",
                                                "sense_id": "c53ec887-0d67-3f31-aae9-a107b4ec946f",
                                                "text": "Where the radio-wave signals of the two radio stations interfere the listener hears nothing but noise."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "68cb906e-0c72-39c0-8f18-a512f3743908",
                                        "entry_id": "31633c1b-7496-3a25-a49d-7e0bccab2fe8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To strike one foot against the opposite foot or ankle in using the legs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of horses"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e155443d-a3aa-3687-b797-3bcf6915023d",
                                        "entry_id": "31633c1b-7496-3a25-a49d-7e0bccab2fe8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To sexually molest, especially of a child."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd3eeea6-10c0-4b48-990b-a1b646e10818",
                                                "sense_id": "e155443d-a3aa-3687-b797-3bcf6915023d",
                                                "text": "The investigation found the girls had been interfered with."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
